# Copy to .context/gate1.env — .context/ is in .git/info/exclude (not .gitignore)
# so the signing key survives branch switches in this clone.
#
# Full per-platform setup and signing instructions (macOS, Windows, Debian,
# Fedora, Arch), key rotation, and troubleshooting:
#   wiki/gate1/signing-instructions.md
#
# Point this at the private key, or at a .pub file when an agent holds the
# private half (macOS Secretive, ssh-agent, a smartcard). ~ and $HOME are
# expanded; nothing else is — the file is parsed literally, never shell-evaluated.
#
# To change a frozen test: copy wiki/gate1/unfreeze-request.template.md to a
# dated request, fill its evidence and authorization, edit the oracle, then run
# node scripts/approve-gate1.js. The first run prints the exact digest needed
# for --confirm-digest-delta; no frozen bytes change until that confirmation.
#
# After rotating the key you MUST also update the GATE1_FINGERPRINT repository
# secret on GitHub, or the gate1-pin CI check fails on every pull request.
RIG_GATE1_SIGNING_KEY= path-to-key
